---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { SITE_ORIGIN, WORKSPACE_ORIGIN } from '../config';
---
<Site title="About the toolbox" description="Domos Tools is an original IT-first collection of sixteen focused utilities, with separate local workspaces and explicit public diagnostics.">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Small tools / deliberate choices</p><h1>Built for the in-between work.</h1><p class="lede">Not every task needs a platform. Sometimes you just need to inspect one header, compare two snippets or work out where a subnet ends.</p></header>
    <div class="article-grid"><article class="article"><h2>Sixteen jobs, one clear approach</h2><p>Domos Tools groups a fixed collection of utilities around real IT tasks: networking, security and identity, development data, encoding, and scheduling. Each has a purpose-built interface, visible errors and a practical guide. You do not need an account.</p>
      <h2>Separate reading from doing</h2><p>This public site at <code>{new URL(SITE_ORIGIN).hostname}</code> contains the directory and guides. Interactive workspaces live at <code>{new URL(WORKSPACE_ORIGIN).hostname}</code>. Live diagnostic requests go only to the configured API. Crossing into a workspace loads a fresh document.</p>
      <h2>Clear limits are part of the product</h2><p>JWT decoding never becomes verification. Email policies are DNS observations, not deliverability guarantees. A failed DNS lookup is not a fabricated empty success. Local computation has explicit input, output and worker execution limits.</p><p>The frozen first-release contract supports regex match inspection rather than replacement, and subnet JSON import with JSON/CSV export rather than CSV import. The interfaces state those boundaries instead of silently providing incompatible behavior.</p>
      <h2>Original work, familiar jobs</h2><p>The need for a good toolbox is familiar. The Domos interface, guides, illustrations and brand are original; functional inspiration does not mean copying another site's source or design. The implementation builds on established open-source libraries whose notices are maintained with the project.</p>
      <h2>Advertising readiness, not advertising activation</h2><p>The public layout includes an optional, clearly labeled reserved sponsorship component, disabled by default. It contains no advertiser, publisher ID, script or tracking request. Workspaces have no advertising component at all.</p><p>Enabling real advertising is a separate product and compliance decision: approved publisher credentials, a reviewed consent path, placement and accessibility review, jurisdiction-specific requirements and a new security-policy review must come first. No ad vendor is activated by this release.</p>
    </article><aside class="guide-aside"><h3>Pick a small thing to finish.</h3><a class="button primary" href="/tools/">Browse the tools &rarr;</a><a href="/guides/">Learn how to read the results</a><a href="/privacy/">Understand the privacy boundary</a></aside></div>
  </div>
</Site>
